---

# 🎯 GOAL

Load data in chunks when user reaches bottom instead of loading everything.

Example:

* Page 1 → 20 items
* Scroll → Page 2 → next 20
* Continue...

---

# 🧠 CORE IDEA (INTERVIEW ONE-LINER)

> Infinite scrolling is implemented by observing a sentinel element using IntersectionObserver and fetching paginated data when it becomes visible.

Why better than scroll event?

❌ scroll → fires 100s times/sec
✅ IntersectionObserver → async, GPU optimized, no layout thrash

---

# 📐 ARCHITECTURE FLOW

```
UI List
   ↓
Sentinel div (last element)
   ↓
IntersectionObserver detects visibility
   ↓
Fetch next page API
   ↓
Append data
   ↓
Re-render
```

