# ⚛️ REACT IMPLEMENTATION (SCALABLE + PERFORMANT)

### 👉 Using functional component + hooks

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from "react";

/*
  InfiniteScroll Component
  ------------------------
  Loads data page by page as user scrolls
*/
export default function InfiniteScroll() {

  // =============================
  // STATE MANAGEMENT
  // =============================

  // Holds all loaded items
  const [items, setItems] = useState([]);

  // Current page number
  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);

  // Indicates whether more data exists on server
  const [hasMore, setHasMore] = useState(true);

  // Shows loading spinner while fetching
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

  // Reference to the sentinel DOM element
  const loaderRef = useRef(null);


  // =============================
  // API FETCH FUNCTION
  // =============================

  const fetchData = useCallback(async () => {

    // Prevent duplicate calls if already loading
    if (loading || !hasMore) return;

    // Start loading
    setLoading(true);

    try {

      // Simulating API call (replace with real API)
      const response = await fetch(
        `/api/items?page=${page}&limit=20`
      );

      // Convert response to JSON
      const result = await response.json();

      /*
        result.data   -> new items
        result.hasMore -> whether more pages exist
      */

      // Append new data to old data
      setItems(prevItems => [...prevItems, ...result.data]);

      // Update if more data exists
      setHasMore(result.hasMore);

      // Move to next page
      setPage(prevPage => prevPage + 1);

    } catch (error) {

      // Log error for debugging
      console.error("Fetch failed:", error);

    } finally {

      // Stop loading spinner
      setLoading(false);
    }

  }, [page, loading, hasMore]);


  // =============================
  // INTERSECTION OBSERVER SETUP
  // =============================

  useEffect(() => {

    // If no more data, stop observing
    if (!hasMore) return;

    // Create new observer
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(

      // Callback runs when sentinel visibility changes
      (entries) => {

        // First entry = our sentinel div
        const entry = entries[0];

        // If sentinel is visible in viewport
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {

          // Fetch next batch
          fetchData();
        }
      },

      {
        // Trigger when 100px before reaching bottom
        rootMargin: "100px",
        threshold: 0.1
      }
    );

    // Start observing sentinel element
    if (loaderRef.current) {
      observer.observe(loaderRef.current);
    }

    // Cleanup on unmount
    return () => observer.disconnect();

  }, [fetchData, hasMore]);


  // =============================
  // INITIAL LOAD
  // =============================

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchData(); // load first page
  }, []);


  // =============================
  // RENDER
  // =============================

  return (
    <div style={{ padding: "20px" }}>

      {/* Render each item */}
      {items.map(item => (

        <div
          key={item.id}
          style={{
            padding: "12px",
            marginBottom: "10px",
            border: "1px solid #ccc"
          }}
        >
          {item.name}
        </div>

      ))}

      {/* Sentinel element */}
      <div ref={loaderRef} />

      {/* Loader */}
      {loading && <p>Loading more...</p>}

      {/* End message */}
      {!hasMore && <p>No more data</p>}

    </div>
  );
}
```

---

# 🔍 DRY RUN (IMPORTANT FOR INTERVIEW)

### Initial render:

page = 1
items = []

→ fetchData() called
→ API returns page 1 data
→ items = [1..20]
→ page becomes 2

---

### User scrolls down:

Sentinel visible

→ observer triggers
→ fetch page 2
→ append items

Now:

items = [1..40]
page = 3

---

### Continues until:

hasMore = false
→ observer stops

---

# 🚀 PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATIONS (INTERVIEW POINTS)

### ✅ No scroll event

(scroll = heavy)

### ✅ useCallback

Prevents observer recreation

### ✅ Pagination

No massive payload

### ✅ Append instead of replace

No full rerender

---

### Optional advanced:

👉 Wrap list items with React.memo
👉 Virtualize huge list (react-window)

---

# 📊 TIME & SPACE COMPLEXITY

### Fetching

Each page fetch → O(k) where k = page size

Total over n items → O(n)

---

### Rendering

Without virtualization → O(n) DOM nodes

With virtualization → O(visible items)

---

# ⚠️ EDGE CASES (INTERVIEWERS ASK)

✅ API slow → show loader
✅ API fails → retry / error UI
✅ User scrolls fast → loading guard prevents duplicate calls
✅ Empty response

---

# 🔐 SECURITY NOTES

• Never trust client pagination
• Server validates page params
• Rate limit API

